240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 845 0 R
/E (Transition to Renewables: Balancing energy access with sustainability goals in Africa presents significant challenges due to underdeveloped infrastructure and the high costs of renewable energy projects. Many African nations lack the grid infrastructure required to support large-scale renewable energy integration, which limits their ability to provide reliable electricity to underserved populations. The initial capital outlay for renewable technologies, such as solar and wind, remains prohibitively high for many countries, despite global cost reductions. Securing funding is further hindered by limited access to international capital markets and the perceived risks of investing in emerging economies. The intermittency of renewable energy sources also necessitates investment in storage solutions and grid stabilisation technologies, which increases overall costs. Regulatory Barriers: Weak regulatory frameworks hinder green financing and ESG implementation.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
