/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (   Expanding Credit Access: The use of alternative credit scoring models offers a transformative opportunity to bridge the financial inclusion gap, particularly for women and small-scale entrepreneurs across Africa. Traditional credit systems often exclude individuals without formal financial histories, leaving many unable to access loans or other financial products. Alternative models, which leverage data such as transaction patterns, mobile phone usage, and utility payments, provide a more inclusive approach to assessing creditworthiness. These methods allow financial institutions to extend credit to individuals traditionally excluded from formal banking.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (   For women entrepreneurs, who face additional barriers such as gender bias and limited property ownership, these models can be particularly impactful. By enabling access to affordable credit, alternative scoring systems can empower small businesses, stimulate local economies, and promote economic equality. Collaboration between fintech companies, banks, and policymakers is essential to scale these solutions effectively.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
