/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Mobile Money A technology that allows users to store, send, and receive money through their mobile phones. Widely used in Africa to bridge financial inclusion gaps, it enables access to banking services without a traditional bank account. Green Bonds Debt instruments issued to finance projects with environmental benefits, such as renewable energy installations or sustainable urban development projects. They offer a way for investors to contribute to sustainability goals. Financial Inclusion The process of ensuring individuals and businesses, particularly those in underserved or rural areas, have access to useful and affordable financial products and services, such as banking, credit, and insurance. Public-Private Partnerships \(PPPs\) Collaborative arrangements between government entities and private sector organizations to fund and operate projects, particularly in infrastructure or service delivery. Cybersecurity The practice of protecting systems, networks, and data from digital attacks, theft, and damage. In fintech, it ensures user trust and safeguards sensitive financial information.)
/E (Mobile Money A technology that allows users to store, send, and receive money through their mobile phones. Widely used in Africa to bridge financial inclusion gaps, it enables access to banking services without a traditional bank account. Green Bonds Debt instruments issued to finance projects with environmental benefits, such as renewable energy installations or sustainable urban development projects. They offer a way for investors to contribute to sustainability goals. Financial Inclusion The process of ensuring individuals and businesses, particularly those in underserved or rural areas, have access to useful and affordable financial products and services, such as banking, credit, and insurance. Public-Private Partnerships \(PPPs\) Collaborative arrangements between government entities and private sector organizations to fund and operate projects, particularly in infrastructure or service delivery. Cybersecurity The practice of protecting systems, networks, and data from digital attacks, theft, and damage. In fintech, it ensures user trust and safeguards sensitive financial information.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
